---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="How this site handles your visit, analytics, and contact form data."
>
  <div class="font-sans text-text">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <!-- Draft from the security planner, adapted for ADR-0008 Amendment 1.
         Open decision: the user edits the wording. -->
    <section id="experience">
      <h2>Your visit becomes a piece of sound and image</h2>
      <p>
        From the first page, this browser tab keeps a record of your visit. When
        you press Time to Say Goodbye, the record plays back once as sound and
        image. Then it is deleted.
      </p>
      <p>The record holds:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>your clicks and taps, as a cell on a coarse grid of the screen;</li>
        <li>
          your pointer position on the same grid, at most ten times a second;
        </li>
        <li>how far you scroll;</li>
        <li>
          the time of each key press, rounded to a tenth of a second. It never
          holds the key.
        </li>
        <li>the pages that you open, as the path only;</li>
        <li>when you hide the tab or change the theme.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        It holds nothing that you type or point at in a form field, such as the
        contact form.
      </p>
      <p>
        On your first page, the site also makes a random key from random
        numbers, the time, your timezone, your theme, your screen size, and the
        type of page you came from (none, this site, or another site). The site
        keeps the key only, not these values.
      </p>
      <p>
        The record stays in the session storage of this tab. The site sends it
        to no server and to no third party. I never receive it, and it cannot
        identify you to me.
      </p>
      <p>
        The site deletes the record after Time to Say Goodbye. Your browser
        deletes it when you close the tab. If a browser restores the tab later,
        the site deletes a record that is more than 30 minutes old.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can read the record in the developer tools of your browser, under
        Session Storage, at the key <code>experience:visit</code>.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        This site does not use analytics yet. When it does, it will use{' '}
        <a
          href="https://www.goatcounter.com/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >
          GoatCounter
        </a>
        , which counts visits without cookies and without personal data. This
        page will say so before that starts.
      </p>
      <p>
        Your choice of light or dark theme is saved in your own browser. It
        never leaves your device.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Contact form</h2>
      <p>
        When you submit the contact form, your name, email address, and message
        are sent to me via{' '}
        <a href="https://resend.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          Resend
        </a>
        , a third-party email service based in the US. Resend keeps the message
        for up to 30 days to deliver it. The site does not store your message,
        and I use it only to reply to you.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
